<blocks app="Snap! 12, https://snap.berkeley.edu" version="2"><palette><category name="Modular" color="120,60,160,1"/></palette><block-definition s="load modular synth primitives" type="command" category="Modular" helper="true"><header></header><code></code><translations></translations><inputs></inputs><script><block s="doApplyExtension"><l>src_load(url)</l><list><l>libraries/modular/modular.js</l></list></block></script></block-definition><block-definition s="create %&apos;type&apos; module named %&apos;name&apos;" type="command" category="Modular"><comment x="0" y="0" w="280" collapsed="false">Creates a new synthesizer module and gives it a name. The name is used by all other blocks to refer to this module. Creating a module with a name that already exists replaces the old module.&#xD;&#xD;oscillator: makes the sound. Inputs: pitch (semitones added to the knobs), trigger (restarts the wave). Outputs: saw, square, triangle, sine. Knobs: octave (-4 to 4), tune (semitones, -48 to 48), pulse width (0 to 1, shape of the square output). With octave and tune at 0 it plays middle C.&#xD;&#xD;filter: removes high frequencies. Inputs: input (sound), cutoff (semitones added to the knob). Output: output. Knobs: cutoff (Hz, where the filter starts cutting), resonance (0 to 1, emphasis at the cutoff; above 0.8 the filter sings on its own).&#xD;&#xD;volume: sets loudness. Inputs: input (sound), level (added to the knob). Output: output. Knob: level (0 to 1).&#xD;&#xD;envelope: makes a control signal that rises when a key is held and falls when it is released. Input: key held. Output: output (0 to amount). Knobs: attack, decay, release (seconds), sustain (0 to 1), amount (the peak; use 1 for a level, 12 for an octave of pitch or cutoff).&#xD;&#xD;wobble: makes a slow repeating control signal. Input: trigger (restarts the cycle). Output: output (-amount to +amount). Knobs: wave (sine, triangle, saw, square), speed (cycles per second), amount.&#xD;&#xD;A module named &quot;speaker&quot; always exists. Patch into its &quot;input&quot; jack to hear a signal. Its only knob is volume (0 to 1).</comment><header></header><code></code><translations></translations><inputs><input type="%s" readonly="true">oscillator<options>oscillator&#xD;filter&#xD;volume&#xD;envelope&#xD;wobble</options></input><input type="%s">osc1</input></inputs><script><custom-block s="load modular synth primitives"></custom-block><block s="doApplyExtension"><l>syn_create(type, name)</l><list><block var="type"/><block var="name"/></list></block></script></block-definition><block-definition s="delete module %&apos;name&apos;" type="command" category="Modular"><comment x="0" y="0" w="200" collapsed="false">Removes a module and all cables plugged into it.</comment><header></header><code></code><translations></translations><inputs><input type="%s"><options>§_ext_syn_names</options></input></inputs><script><custom-block s="load modular synth primitives"></custom-block><block s="doApplyExtension"><l>syn_delete(name)</l><list><block var="name"/></list></block></script></block-definition><block-definition s="delete all modules" type="command" category="Modular"><comment x="0" y="0" w="200" collapsed="false">Removes every module except the speaker, and silences the synth.</comment><header></header><code></code><translations></translations><inputs></inputs><script><custom-block s="load modular synth primitives"></custom-block><block s="doApplyExtension"><l>syn_clear()</l><list></list></block></script></block-definition><block-definition s="connect %&apos;module&apos; %&apos;output&apos; to %&apos;module2&apos; %&apos;input&apos;" type="command" category="Modular"><comment x="0" y="0" w="280" collapsed="false">Plugs a cable from an output jack of one module into an input jack of another. Several cables may share one input; their signals are added, which is how sounds are mixed. A control cable into a knob&apos;s jack (pitch, cutoff, level) adds to that knob.&#xD;&#xD;Example: connect osc1 saw to filter1 input</comment><header></header><code></code><translations></translations><inputs><input type="%s"><options>§_ext_syn_names</options></input><input type="%s"><options>§_ext_syn_outputs</options></input><input type="%s"><options>§_ext_syn_names</options></input><input type="%s"><options>§_ext_syn_inputs</options></input></inputs><script><custom-block s="load modular synth primitives"></custom-block><block s="doApplyExtension"><l>syn_connect(module, output, module, input)</l><list><block var="module"/><block var="output"/><block var="module2"/><block var="input"/></list></block></script></block-definition><block-definition s="disconnect %&apos;module&apos; %&apos;input&apos;" type="command" category="Modular"><comment x="0" y="0" w="220" collapsed="false">Unplugs every cable from an input jack of a module.</comment><header></header><code></code><translations></translations><inputs><input type="%s"><options>§_ext_syn_names</options></input><input type="%s"><options>§_ext_syn_inputs</options></input></inputs><script><custom-block s="load modular synth primitives"></custom-block><block s="doApplyExtension"><l>syn_disconnect(module, input)</l><list><block var="module"/><block var="input"/></list></block></script></block-definition><block-definition s="set %&apos;module&apos; %&apos;knob&apos; to %&apos;value&apos;" type="command" category="Modular"><comment x="0" y="0" w="260" collapsed="false">Turns a knob of a module to the given value. Values outside the knob&apos;s range are clipped. The wave knob of a wobble takes a name: sine, triangle, saw or square.</comment><header></header><code></code><translations></translations><inputs><input type="%s"><options>§_ext_syn_names</options></input><input type="%s"><options>§_ext_syn_knobs</options></input><input type="%s"></input></inputs><script><custom-block s="load modular synth primitives"></custom-block><block s="doApplyExtension"><l>syn_set(module, knob, value)</l><list><block var="module"/><block var="knob"/><block var="value"/></list></block></script></block-definition><block-definition s="%&apos;module&apos; %&apos;knob&apos;" type="reporter" category="Modular"><comment x="0" y="0" w="200" collapsed="false">Reports the current position of a knob of a module.</comment><header></header><code></code><translations></translations><inputs><input type="%s"><options>§_ext_syn_names</options></input><input type="%s"><options>§_ext_syn_knobs</options></input></inputs><script><custom-block s="load modular synth primitives"></custom-block><block s="doReport"><block s="reportApplyExtension"><l>syn_get(module, knob)</l><list><block var="module"/><block var="knob"/></list></block></block></script></block-definition><block-definition s="key held on %&apos;module&apos; %&apos;held?&apos;" type="command" category="Modular"><comment x="0" y="0" w="260" collapsed="false">Tells an envelope module that a key is being held (true) or has been released (false), in place of a cable in its key held input. Holding starts the attack, releasing starts the release.</comment><header></header><code></code><translations></translations><inputs><input type="%s"><options>§_ext_syn_names</options></input><input type="%b"></input></inputs><script><custom-block s="load modular synth primitives"></custom-block><block s="doApplyExtension"><l>syn_key(module, bool)</l><list><block var="module"/><block var="held?"/></list></block></script></block-definition><block-definition s="modules" type="reporter" category="Modular"><comment x="0" y="0" w="200" collapsed="false">Reports the names of all existing modules.</comment><header></header><code></code><translations></translations><inputs></inputs><script><custom-block s="load modular synth primitives"></custom-block><block s="doReport"><block s="reportApplyExtension"><l>syn_modules()</l><list></list></block></block></script></block-definition><block-definition s="note %&apos;number&apos; as pitch" type="reporter" category="Modular"><comment x="0" y="0" w="260" collapsed="false">Converts a MIDI note number into semitones above middle C, the unit of an oscillator&apos;s tune knob and pitch input. Middle C (60) gives 0.</comment><header></header><code></code><translations></translations><inputs><input type="%n">60</input></inputs><script><block s="doReport"><block s="reportDifference"><block var="number"/><l>60</l></block></block></script></block-definition></blocks>
